  "documents": {
   "paper.md": [
    "# Widget Readings on a Level Bench",
    "",
    "## Abstract",
    "",
    "We describe repeated readings of small widgets on a level bench. The readings were taken under the same conditions on three days. This document is synthetic prose written for software tests and reports no real experiment.",
    "",
    "## 1 Methods",
    "",
    "Each widget was placed against the stop and read with the same instrument. The observer checked the scale against a reference block before every reading.",
    "",
    "## 2 Results",
    "",
    "The blue widgets read the same on every day. The green widgets differed by less than the smallest division of the scale.",
    "",
    "$$ E = m c^{2} \\tag{(1)} $$",
    "",
    "The current was logged every hour.",
    "",
    "| Hour | Current (mA) |",
    "| --- | --- |",
    "| 1 | 4.5 |",
    "| 2 | 9.0 |",
    "",
    "Caption: Table 1: Current by hour.",
    "",
    "Figure: Figure 1: The bench, the instrument and the widgets.",
    "",
    "Figure description: A photograph of the bench with the instrument clamped at the left and three widgets in a row. The scale under them is marked from 0 to 40 mm.",
    "",
    "The readings held across the week and no widget moved.",
    "",
    "The stop block was checked against the reference block at the end of each day. No check moved the stop by more than the smallest division of the scale, so every reading was kept."
   ]
  },
